# ==============================================================================
# VARIÁVEIS DE AMBIENTE E TESTE
# ==============================================================================

# URL base (use http://localhost:5077 caso rode no perfil HTTP sem SSL)
@baseUrl = https://localhost:7049

# Dados do usuário de teste (/auth)
@userName = Usuário Teste
@userEmail = teste@exemplo.com
@userPassword = Password123!

# Cliente Web (Authorization Code + PKCE e Refresh Token)
@webClientId = web-client
@webClientSecret = dev-secret-123
@redirectUri = http%3A%2F%2Flocalhost%3A3000%2Fcallback
@scopes = openid%20email%20profile%20offline_access

# Par PKCE válido (S256 = BASE64URL(SHA256(code_verifier)))
@codeVerifier = dBjftJeZ4CVP-mB92K27uhbUJU1p1r_wW1gFWFOEjXk
@codeChallenge = E9Melhoa2OwvFrEMTJguCHaoeK1t8URWbuGJSstw-cM

# Preencha com os valores retornados nas etapas 3 e 4 antes de executar as etapas seguintes
@authorizationCode = COLE_AQUI_O_CODIGO_DE_AUTORIZACAO
@accessToken = COLE_AQUI_O_ACCESS_TOKEN
@refreshToken = COLE_AQUI_O_REFRESH_TOKEN

# Cliente M2M (Client Credentials)
@serviceClientId = service-client
@serviceClientSecret = service-secret-123


### 1.1 [Health Check] Verificar status do serviço
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### 1.2 [OIDC Discovery] Obter metadados OpenID Connect
GET {{baseUrl}}/.well-known/openid-configuration

### 1.3 [OIDC Discovery] Obter chaves públicas (JWKS)
GET {{baseUrl}}/.well-known/jwks


### 2.1 [Auth] Registrar um usuário de teste
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "{{userName}}",
  "email": "{{userEmail}}",
  "password": "{{userPassword}}"
}

### 2.2 [Auth] Fazer login (emite o cookie temporário .AuthService.Session)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{userEmail}}",
  "password": "{{userPassword}}"
}

### 2.3 [Auth] Fazer logout (descarta cookie e revoga refresh_tokens do usuário)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}


### 3.1 [Authorization Code + PKCE] Solicitar authorization_code (requer cookie da etapa 2.2)
# Dica: copie o parâmetro "code" do header "Location" na resposta 302 para @authorizationCode no topo.
GET {{baseUrl}}/connect/authorize?client_id={{webClientId}}&redirect_uri={{redirectUri}}&response_type=code&scope={{scopes}}&code_challenge={{codeChallenge}}&code_challenge_method=S256&state=xyz123

### 3.2 [Authorization Code + PKCE] Trocar authorization_code por access_token, id_token e refresh_token
POST {{baseUrl}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=authorization_code&client_id={{webClientId}}&client_secret={{webClientSecret}}&code={{authorizationCode}}&redirect_uri={{redirectUri}}&code_verifier={{codeVerifier}}


### 4.1 [Refresh Token] Renovar tokens com rotação automática
# Dica: copie o "refresh_token" da resposta 3.2 para @refreshToken no topo.
POST {{baseUrl}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=refresh_token&client_id={{webClientId}}&client_secret={{webClientSecret}}&refresh_token={{refreshToken}}


### 5.1 [Client Credentials] Obter access_token M2M entre microsserviços
POST {{baseUrl}}/connect/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&client_id={{serviceClientId}}&client_secret={{serviceClientSecret}}


### 6.1 [Revocation] Revogar refresh_token (RFC 7009)
POST {{baseUrl}}/connect/revoke
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

token={{refreshToken}}&token_type_hint=refresh_token&client_id={{webClientId}}&client_secret={{webClientSecret}}


### 7.1 [UserInfo] Obter perfil atualizado do usuário autenticado (OIDC)
# Dica: copie o "access_token" obtido na etapa 3.2 ou 4.1 para @accessToken no topo.
GET {{baseUrl}}/connect/userinfo
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###
